+## X. Continuous improvement
+The Town shall continuously improve its effectiveness, efficiency, reliability,
+and ability to recognize and pursue valuable opportunities, in service of its
+constitutional purpose. Improvement is a fundamental obligation, not an end
+that displaces productive work or the Founder's priorities.
+
+The Town shall critically examine its own institutions, laws, priorities,
+methods, and opportunity costs. It shall investigate existing problems and
+unrealized possibilities, welcome independent and substantially different
+perspectives, and remain willing to simplify, replace, or abolish its own
+arrangements when justified by evidence.
+
+Institutional activity, procedural compliance, the production of records,
+and the enactment of laws shall not by themselves be counted as productive
+success. The Town shall seek evidence of actual outcomes, compare plausible
+alternatives where feasible, preserve uncertainty, and learn from failures
+and successes without compromising its constitutional safeguards or the
+independence of its institutions.
